    "durationMs": 169866,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and fully verified. Summary of what I built and confirmed:\n\n**Implementation** (Spring Boot 3.4.5 / Java 21, package `bench.app`)\n- `POST /links` — validates URL (absolute http/https with host) and optional code (`[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}`), generates a unique 8-char code when omitted, returns `201 {\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\"}` with the URL unchanged; duplicate custom code → `409`\n- `GET /links/{code}` → `200` or `404` with `{\"error\": ...}`\n- `GET /r/{code}` → `302` with exact `Location` header; clicks incremented via an atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1` so each redirect counts exactly once\n- `GET /links` → `{\"items\": [...], \"total\": n}` in ascending creation order\n- Malformed JSON, missing/invalid URL, invalid code → `422` with an `error` field (via `@RestControllerAdvice`)\n- **Persistence**: Spring Data JPA + Flyway migration (`V1__create_links.sql`), Postgres settings parsed from the `DATABASE_URL` env var by an `EnvironmentPostProcessor` (registered in `spring.factories`) — no hard-coded credentials\n\n**Verified with live curl tests**: all happy paths, all 422 variants, 409 duplicate, 404 unknown codes, click counting across two redirects, and a full server restart showing clicks (`2`) and rows surviving — Flyway correctly reported \"Schema is up to date\" on restart.\n\n**Startup**: `sh start.sh` builds `target/app.jar` if missing (deps already installed in `~/.m2`) and runs it in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; Flyway applies pending migrations before the server binds. README documents all of it.\n\nI removed all my test rows from the `links` table and stopped the dev server, so the suite starts against a clean, migrated database."
